e104†Robert A. Scott cite105†ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0003-3634-3016†orcid.org ^{cite26†6 },\nL78:   * cite106†Erin N. Smith ^{cite107†23 },\nL79:   * cite108†Sándor Szalma cite109†ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0001-7591-3902†orcid.org ^{cite107†23 },\nL80:   * cite110†Dawn M. Waterworth cite111†ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0002-9226-1317†orcid.org ^{cite112†24 },\nL81:   * cite113†Lyndon J. Mitnaul ^{cite43†12 },\nL82:   * cite114†Joseph D. Szustakowski cite115†ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0001-7900-3973†orcid.org ^{cite33†8 }^{ cite116†na2 },\nL83:   * cite117†Bradford W. Gibson cite118†ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0003-3745-1940†orcid.org ^{cite24†5 }^{ cite116†na2 },\nL84:   * cite119†Melissa R. Miller ^{cite17†2 }^{ cite116†na2 } &\nL85:   * …\nL86:   * cite120†Christopher D. Whelan cite121†ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0003-0308-5583†orcid.org ^{cite14†1 ,cite122†25 }^{ cite116†na2 }\nL87: Show authors\nL88: cite123†Nature volume 622, pages 329–338 (2023)\nL89: \nL90: cite124†Save article L91: \nL92: cite1†View saved research L93: \nL94:   * 276k Accesses\nL95: \nL96:   * 2072 Citations\nL97: \nL98:   * 364 Altmetric\nL99: \nL100:   * cite125†Metrics details L101: ## Abstract\nL102: The Pharma Proteomics Project is a precompetitive biopharmaceutical consortium characterizing the plasma proteomic profiles of 54,219 UK Biobank participants. Here we provide a detailed summary of this initiative, including technical and biological validations, insights into proteomic disease signatures, and prediction modelling for various demographic and health indicators.\nL103: We present comprehensive protein quantitative trait locus (pQTL) mapping of 2,923 proteins that identifies 14,287 primary genetic associations, of which 81% are previously undescribed, alongside ancestry-specific pQTL mapping in non-European individuals. The study provides an updated characterization of the genetic architecture of the plasma proteome, contextualized with projected pQTL discovery rates as sample sizes and proteomic assay coverages increase over time.\nL104: We offer extensive insights into trans pQTLs across multiple biological domains, highlight genetic influences on ligand–receptor interactions and pathway perturbations across a diverse collection of cytokines and complement networks, and illustrate long-range epistatic effects of ABO blood group and FUT2 secretor status on proteins with gastrointestinal tissue-enriched expression.\nL105: We demonstrate the utility of these data for drug discovery by extending the genetic proxied effects of protein targets, such as PCSK9, on additional endpoints, and disentangle specific genes and proteins perturbed at loci associated with COVID-19 susceptibility.\nL106: This public–private partnership provides the scientific community with an open-access proteomics resource of considerable breadth and depth to help to elucidate the biological mechanisms underlying proteo-genomic discoveries and accelerate the development of biomarkers, predictive models and therapeutics^{cite126†1 }.\nL107: ### Similar content being viewed by others\nL108: \nL109: cite127†Image†media.springernature.com L110: \nL111: ### cite128†Nanoparticle-enriched mass spectrometry proteomics in British South Asians identifies links between genetic variants, plasma protein levels and disease risk L112: \nL113: Article Open access 24 July 2026\nL114: \nL115: cite129†Image†media.springernature.com L116: \nL117: ### cite130†Complex genetic effects linked to plasma protein abundance in the UK Biobank L118: \nL119: Article Open access 14 December 2025\nL120: \nL121: cite131†Image†media.springernature.com L122: ### cite132†Large-scale integration of the plasma proteome with genetics and disease L123: \nL124: Article 02 December 2021\nL125: ## Main\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\npubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37794188/)\nciteturn8view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37794188/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 0\n"
